    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map ldp-export permit 10', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'route-map ldp-export permit 10', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map ldp-export permit 10\\n match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES\\n!\\nip prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES seq 5 permit 10.1.1.2/32\\nip prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES seq 10 permit 2.2.2.9/32\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, we typically use route-maps with prefix-lists to achieve similar functionality to Juniper's policy statements. The exact matching is implicit in the prefix-list entries since we specify /32 masks. The sequence numbers in the prefix-list serve a similar purpose to the terms in Juniper's policy.\", 'trans_template': 'route-map ldp-export permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map ldp-export permit 10\\n match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES\\n!\\nip prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES seq 5 permit 10.1.1.2/32\\nip prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES seq 10 permit 2.2.2.9/32\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, we typically use route-maps with prefix-lists to achieve similar functionality to Juniper's policy statements. The exact matching is implicit in the prefix-list entries since we specify /32 masks. The sequence numbers in the prefix-list serve a similar purpose to the terms in Juniper's policy.\", 'trans_template': 'match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': '!', 'parent_command': [], 'root': '!', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map ldp-export permit 10\\n match ip address prefix-list LDP-