    "['term [parameter2] from route-filter [parameter3]/[parameter4] [parameter5]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map ldp-export permit 10', 'parent_command': ['route-map ldp-export permit 10'], 'root': 'route-map ldp-export permit 10', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map ldp-export permit 10\\n match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, you would also need to create the prefix-list separately:\\n```\\nip prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES seq 5 permit 10.1.1.2/32\\n```\\n\\nThe Juniper `route-filter` with `exact` is equivalent to a Cisco prefix-list with an exact match (same prefix length). The `term 1` in Juniper translates to sequence number 10 in Cisco's route-map (Cisco typically uses increments of 10).\", 'trans_template': 'route-map ldp-export permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES', 'parent_command': ['route-map ldp-export permit 10'], 'root': 'route-map ldp-export permit 10', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map ldp-export permit 10\\n match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, you would also need to create the prefix-list separately:\\n```\\nip prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES seq 5 permit 10.1.1.2/32\\n```\\n\\nThe Juniper `route-filter` with `exact` is equivalent to a Cisco prefix-list with an exact match (same prefix length). The `term 1` in Juniper translates to sequence number 10 in Cisco's route-map (Cisco typically uses increments of 10).\", 'trans_template': 'match ip address prefix-list LDP-PREFIXES'}]]": 1,
